{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"The overflow fallback is correct on deliberately adversarial all-to-one routing and costs under a microsecond on normal workloads. I’m doing one last local-only throughput experiment: unrolling the gather two expert rows at a time to expose independent HBM reads and hide the per-row address latency. I’ll keep it only if repeated timings improve."}}
